      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "So-called alternative methods are surely not the solution for the therapy of chronic pain. Although those methods may often produce a marked placebo effect, it must be pointed out that so far there has not been any proof of a specific effect. At some methods, especially acupuncture, a therapeutic effect seems possible. Further carefully planned clinical studies are necessary. Finally the therapy with such unproofed methods often causes high costs that contrast to the effectivity."},
